{"id": "csot-2026-07-16-011", "date": "2026-07-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": ["csot", "tcl"], "customers": ["tcl"], "suppliers": ["csot"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "Lenovo and MSI launch the first consumer products to utilize TCL CSOT's inkjet printed OLED panels", "content": "<p>A few days ago we reported that TCL CSOT is launching commercial production of inkjet printed OLED panels at the company's 5.5-Gen line, and today two companies formally announced the first products to utilize these panels. This is an exciting moment for the OLED industry - we already had commercial inkjet production by JOLED years ago, but the company did not manage to reach full-scale production. Hopefully TCL CSOT with its T8 large-scale 8.6-Gen line will fare much better.</p><img src=\"htt", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/lenovo-and-msi-launch-first-consumer-products-utilize-tcl-csots-inkjet-printed", "type": "rss"}]}
